  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The political landscape in Indonesia is shifting as focus intensifies on the selection of a new vice president to serve alongside President Prabowo Subianto. As discussions continue, Sugiono and Amran have emerged as the primary subjects of political debate among various factions within the People's Consultative Assembly. Several regional Gerindra party chapters, including those in West Nusa Tenggara and East Jakarta, have publicly endorsed Sugiono, citing his capacity to represent younger generations and articulate public interests. Concurrently, broader political interest is surfacing, with members of the Regional Representative Council and multiple party factions evaluating their stances. To ensure commitment to the selection process, both Sugiono and Amran are expected to formalize their participation by signing official statements confirming they will not withdraw during the ongoing vice presidential appointment proceedings.",
